{
  "id": "ghlEmailSender01",
  "name": "[GHL Store Automation] | Email Sender",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "e-ifgmail",
      "name": "Gmail Mode Selected?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        272,
        560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "g1",
              "leftValue": "={{ ['gmail', 'both'].includes($json.email_mode) }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e-gmail",
      "name": "Send Email Via Gmail",
      "webhookId": "de03af21-8f49-4fba-8cb1-432f0cc8dffb",
      "disabled": false,
      "notes": "Sends with the 'Gmail account' credential when email_mode is gmail or both.",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        512,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "={{ $('Receive Email Request').first().json.to }}",
        "subject": "={{ $('Receive Email Request').first().json.subject }}",
        "emailType": "text",
        "message": "={{ $('Receive Email Request').first().json.body }}",
        "options": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "gmailOAuth2": {
          "id": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "Gmail account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e-ifmailpit",
      "name": "Mailpit Mode Selected?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        800,
        560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "m1",
              "leftValue": "={{ ['mailpit', 'both'].includes($('Receive Email Request').first().json.email_mode) }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e-smtp",
      "name": "Send Email Via Mailpit",
      "webhookId": "cc675168-146e-4ab3-9205-63edfbfc23d3",
      "disabled": false,
      "notes": "Attach the SMTP credential for Mailpit (host mailpit, port 1025, no auth).",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.emailSend",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        1040,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "fromEmail": "={{ $('Receive Email Request').first().json.from_email || 'store@demo.test' }}",
        "toEmail": "={{ $('Receive Email Request').first().json.to }}",
        "subject": "={{ $('Receive Email Request').first().json.subject }}",
        "emailFormat": "text",
        "text": "={{ $('Receive Email Request').first().json.body }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "credentials": {
        "smtp": {
          "id": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "Mailpit SMTP"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e-summary",
      "name": "Summarise Email Result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1488,
        560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const req = $('Receive Email Request').first().json;\nconst sentVia = [];\nconst errors = [];\nif ($('Send Email Via Gmail').isExecuted) {\n  const g = $('Send Email Via Gmail').first().json;\n  if (g.error) errors.push('gmail: ' + String(g.error.message || g.error)); else sentVia.push('gmail');\n}\nif ($('Send Email Via Mailpit').isExecuted) {\n  const m = $('Send Email Via Mailpit').first().json;\n  if (m.error) errors.push('mailpit: ' + String(m.error.message || m.error)); else sentVia.push('mailpit');\n}\nreturn [{ json: { ok: errors.length === 0 && sentVia.length > 0, sent_via: sentVia, error: errors.join(' | '), to: req.to } }];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e-trigger",
      "name": "Receive Email Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        48,
        560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "inputSource": "passthrough"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e-t",
      "name": "Title Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Email Sender\n\nOne place that sends every email for the store automation. The caller passes the recipient, subject, body and an email mode; this workflow sends through Gmail (real delivery), through Mailpit (local test inbox), or both.\n\n**Called by:** the four handler workflows. **Standalone-capable:** no.\n\n**Email modes:** gmail = real email only, mailpit = local test inbox only, both = real email plus a copy in Mailpit.\n\n**Sections:** 1. Send through Gmail. 2. Send through Mailpit. 3. Report the result.\n\n**Input:** to, subject, body, email_mode, from_email. **Output:** ok, sent_via, error, to.\n\n**Credentials:** 'Gmail account' (Gmail OAuth2) on 'Send Email Via Gmail', 'Mailpit SMTP' (host mailpit, port 1025, no authentication) on 'Send Email Via Mailpit'. On a new n8n server, reconnect 'Gmail account' there.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 1720,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e-1",
      "name": "Section 1 Note - Send Through Gmail",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send through Gmail\n\nTriggered by: a handler workflow calling this one (Execute Workflow).\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Receives the email request.\n2. If the mode is gmail or both, sends the email through Gmail. A failure here does not stop the workflow (soft fail); the error is reported in the result.",
        "height": 680,
        "width": 720,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e-2",
      "name": "Section 2 Note - Send Through Mailpit",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        752,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send through Mailpit\n\nTriggered by: runs inline after 'Send through Gmail'.\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. If the mode is mailpit or both, sends the same email by SMTP to the local Mailpit inbox (localhost:8025).\n2. A failure here is also a soft fail and is reported in the result.",
        "height": 680,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e-3",
      "name": "Section 3 Note - Report The Result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1392,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Report the result\n\nTriggered by: runs inline after 'Send through Mailpit'.\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Collects which senders actually ran and whether each succeeded.\n2. Returns ok, sent_via, error and the recipient to the caller.",
        "height": 680,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 5
      }
    }
  ],
